<Project>
  <!--
    qsm-langdev profile: general. Seeded by `qsm-langdev init`; the repo owns
    this file.

    AnalysisMode Default runs the SDK's recommended CA set (verified against
    dotnet 10.0.111). EnforceCodeStyleInBuild turns on the IDE-prefixed style
    rules, but their severity comes from .editorconfig, not from here: without
    the severity line in .editorconfig, IDE rules build clean even with this
    flag on.

    Every analyzer finding gates, and none of them is a warning nobody acts on.
    The gate builds with -p:TreatWarningsAsErrors=false on the command line,
    which beats anything this file says, and counts what the build reports on
    both sides of a commit and a push: one more finding than the reference
    commit blocks. The override is what makes them countable — under
    TreatWarningsAsErrors the build stops at the first one and reports a failed
    build instead of a list, which the gate can only read as a broken run.
    Verified on dotnet 10.0.111: the same file builds to errors with
    TreatWarningsAsErrors set in the project and to CS8603, CA1050 and CA1822
    with the gate's override in place.

    A rule worth suppressing at a call site was the wrong rule to enable: turn
    it off in .editorconfig with the reason, never a #pragma in the code.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <AnalysisLevel>latest</AnalysisLevel>
    <AnalysisMode>Default</AnalysisMode>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
